From a63d335a2f66b29e4ab23497b37bdf349faca105 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jan 2024 15:40:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 458/841] refactor(st): change suffixes for SYSCFG functions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This patch replaces the suffixes "stm32mp1_" and "stm32mp2_" in the two
SYSCFG drivers with "stm32mp_". By using a common suffix for function
names, we can avoid issues or platform compilation flags when a driver
needs to access SYSCFG across different platforms.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git e4f9d7713a3fc8d4ca4a93ec277294e937b9c1d4 refactor(st): change suffixes for SYSCFG functions]
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I24407852c085abd843ef4cdef235c022a5e57a85
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/351769
Domain-Review: Sebastien PASDELOUP <sebastien.pasdeloup-ext@st.com>
Tested-by: Sebastien PASDELOUP <sebastien.pasdeloup-ext@st.com>
Reviewed-by: Sebastien PASDELOUP <sebastien.pasdeloup-ext@st.com>
---
